## What you get

| Feature | Notes |
|---|---|
| Open GPU stack | Panthor DRM + Mesa (Panfrost). KDE composites on GPU; renderer reports `Mali-G610 MC4 (Panfrost)`, not `llvmpipe`. Hardware cursor plane. |
| Open Vulkan | PanVK on Mali-G610, no vendor blob. |
| Hardware video | Rockchip MPP through mpv. `ff2mpv` browser button hands page video to mpv. |
| Hardware video encode | H.264, HEVC and MJPEG on VPU through `h96-encode`. |
| Display | Kernel reads display EDID over GPIO DDC bus; `h96-display detect` lists modes; HDMI 2.0 modes up to 3840x2160 at 60 Hz verified. |
| WiFi 6 | Radio sits on **PCIe**, not SDIO, so WiFi and Ethernet run at same time. Connect with `sudo h96-wifi-connect` or WiFi tray icon. |
| Bluetooth | BCM4362A2 with vendor firmware in image. A2DP out with LDAC, aptX HD, aptX and SBC; headset microphone over HFP. |
| HDMI audio | Default output; S/PDIF optical selectable. |
| Front-panel display | Clock plus Ethernet, WiFi, USB and play icons from live system state (`h96-vfd.service`). |
| NPU | 3 cores, about 6 TOPS. Per-core load through `h96-npu`. Proprietary inference runtime fetched on demand by `h96-npu-setup`, never bundled. |
| Gaming | `h96-steam` installs Steam ARM; `h96-game-mode` with box64, Wine and DXVK for titles outside Steam; `h96-emulators` for GPU emulators; `h96-waydroid` for Android in container. |
| Backup | `h96-backup` and `h96-restore`; backups from v5.0.1 onward restore. |
| SSH | On from first boot. Default login `root` / `1234`. Change it. |

