## Flashing

**Needed:** Linux host, `rkdeveloptool`, USB-A to USB-A data cable, `MiniLoaderAll.bin` and
image from release download. Flashing erases eMMC; back up first (`h96-backup`).

```bash
# 1. Check and decompress
sha256sum -c --ignore-missing SHA256SUMS
xz -dk H96-MAX-V58_Unofficial-Armbian_<version>.img.xz
sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS

# 2. Loader mode: on running box run  sudo reboot loader
#    or pinhole: power off, hold pinhole (rear, between antenna posts),
#    plug cable into black USB2 port, release after about 3 s
rkdeveloptool ld                     # Loader or Maskrom

# 3. From Loader: erase, reset into Maskrom (db is refused in Loader)
rkdeveloptool ef
rkdeveloptool rd
sleep 5
rkdeveloptool ld                     # Maskrom

# 4. Write, read back, compare, reset
rkdeveloptool db MiniLoaderAll.bin
rkdeveloptool wl 0 H96-MAX-V58_Unofficial-Armbian_<version>.img
rkdeveloptool rl 0 <sectors> readback.img   # sectors = image bytes / 512
sha256sum readback.img               # equal to .img sha256
rkdeveloptool rd
```

**Never interrupt `wl` once it starts.** On read-back mismatch, repeat `db` and `wl` before
reset. First boot shows console on HDMI and runs setup before SSH answers; 8.0 beta
reboots once, v7.2 twice. Network can take minutes after reboot, and DHCP address can
change.

```bash
ssh root@<ip>     # password: 1234
```

v7.2 release download includes full flashing guide (`FLASHING.md`), scripted flasher
(`flash.py`) and command reference (`COMMANDS.md`).

